D1 — Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) & Approval Matrix Architecture Purpose

Prevent autonomous overspending and ensure consistent corporate oversight by placing clear decision boundaries, programmatic guards, and escalation paths around the agent.
Key behaviors (plain English)

The agent recommends bookings and changes, but certain costs or rule-violations automatically trigger human approval steps before any booking is completed.
All approval actions and decisions are logged with timestamps and approver identity for auditability.
Approval thresholds (routing rules)

Total cost < USD 1,000
Route to: Line Manager
Action expected: Manager confirms budget and business purpose; approval recorded.
Total cost USD 1,000 – USD 3,000
Route to: Department Head
Action expected: Dept Head verifies policy compliance and approves or escalates.
Total cost USD 3,000 – USD 10,000
Route to: Director
Action expected: Director-level approval required.
Total cost > USD 10,000
Route to: CFO/CEO + Finance Review
Action expected: Formal finance and risk review; decision required before booking.
Hard governance guardrails (non-negotiable)

No Self-Approval (GENERAL-01)
The system blocks any attempt by a requester to approve their own travel.
No Expense Splitting
The system detects and blocks attempts to split invoices or trip legs to avoid thresholds; such attempts are escalated for investigation and rejected if abusive.
Operational details for the HITL flow

Metadata included with every approval request:
Requester, cost breakdown, policy IDs checked, suggested compliant alternatives, and audit token.
Escalation behavior:
If no compliant option exists within caps, the agent produces a clear escalation notice including exact violated Policy IDs and suggested next steps (e.g., request formal exception).
UI / Demo behavior (Streamlit)
Approvers receive an escalation panel showing choices, compliance flags (green/yellow/red), required approval buttons, and an audit log view.
Example approval routing (copyable):
Request total: USD 2,450 → Route: Department Head → Approval required before auto-booking.
